# FIX-CLINIC-OPS-BRANCH-CONTEXT-WA-1 — durable rules

## Working branch scope

1. `App\Modules\RmeOnlineContext\Services\RmeWorkingBranchScope` is the ONLY
   authority for "which RME branches may this workspace read?". Do not re-derive
   branch scope in a controller, repository or Blade view.
2. Context-bound roles are **Admin Klinik, Perawat and Kasir**. Each works from
   one selected branch, chosen through the branch-only online context.
3. **Fail closed.** A context-bound user with no valid context gets an EMPTY
   scope. Never fall back to MAIN, to the first active branch, to the patient's
   branch, or to the whole estate.
4. A request `branch_id` may only NARROW an authorised scope. It may never widen
   it. Never trust a request branch id as authority.
5. Governance roles (Owner, Super Admin, Supervisor RME) and the reporting roles
   keep the full active RME-enabled set — cross-branch analytics are intentional.
6. **Doctor is NOT context-bound by this scope.** The doctor clinical branch
   model (practice branches, `DoctorClinicalBranchResolver`) is a separate
   domain and must not be regressed.
7. Scope applies to lists, counts, aggregates, totals, print and export alike.
   Scoping a table but not its CSV is a leak.

## Document identity

8. A document's clinic identity comes from the branch that OWNS the record, not
   from the viewer's working context and not from a literal in a shared
   template. Printing another branch's record prints that branch's identity.
9. Never invent an address. A branch with no address recorded prints no address
   line — never a placeholder presented as real data, and never another
   branch's address as a fallback.

## Examination completion

10. "Selesai Pemeriksaan" requires `complete_rme_examination` (Doctor, Perawat,
    Supervisor RME; Super Admin via `Gate::before`). Admin Klinik keeps
    registration and room placement but may never close an examination.
11. `cashier_pending → completed` stays cashier-owned: only `RmePaymentService`
    reaches it, once the invoice is settled. Do not add a manual path.
12. Hiding a button is never the boundary. Every hidden action is also denied
    server-side by its own ability.

## Visit list date

13. Daftar Kunjungan defaults to the **clinical** day (`ClinicalClock`,
    Asia/Makassar). Historical visits require an explicit date or range filter.
14. `visit_date` is a clinical calendar date. Stamp it from `ClinicalClock`,
    never from a UTC `today()`/`now()` — they differ for eight hours a day, and
    the same value drives the queue number and the visit number.

## WhatsApp prescription delivery

15. Delivery is server-to-server through Meta's official Cloud API. No `wa.me`,
    no WhatsApp Web, no browser redirect, no deep link.
16. Meta delivers non-template messages only inside an open 24-hour customer
    service window, so a proactive prescription always sends an **approved
    utility template**. Never attempt to bypass that.
17. OFF by default and fail-closed: without credentials the disabled gateway is
    bound and opens no socket.
18. The outbound host is checked against an allowlist and must be HTTPS before
    any request. Redirects are never followed.
19. The access token comes from the environment only. Never log it, never
    persist it, never render it, never return it.
20. Sending is an explicit, confirmed operator action gated by
    `send_prescription_whatsapp` — never automatic on save, finalize or a
    schedule. It is idempotent per prescription + recipient + template.
21. A delivery failure never mutates the prescription or the visit.
22. Send only what belongs on a prescription hand-off. No diagnosis, no clinical
    notes, no KTP/NIK.

## SATUSEHAT

23. SATUSEHAT is **Super Admin only**. One `satusehat.access` gate backs both the
    route group and the sidebar, so the menu and the boundary cannot drift apart.
24. The per-feature SATUSEHAT permissions stay in place: they still tier what a
    Super Admin may do, and some of them gate clinical-diagnosis routes that are
    not part of the SATUSEHAT module. Do not revoke them to "tidy up".

## Tests

25. A Kasir fixture must select a working branch (`rmeMakeKasirActive`), exactly
    as Perawat's did when Perawat became context-bound.
26. Fixtures that assert visit dates, queue numbers or visit numbers use
    `clinicalToday()`, not `today()`.
27. WhatsApp tests are hermetic: `Http::preventStrayRequests()` always, and
    `Http::assertNothingSent()` on every fail-closed path.
